Z||000002||beer_stud_21||11-10-2001||10:41 PM||||Beutiful car John!  I am planning on repainting my car that color red.  I can't believe my car used to be that color.  It's so faded now.  If you got an extra pass side dew wipe I will buy it from you...  I am not going to be replacing mine for a while, but if I can do you the favor I will....<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnF||11-11-2001||08:20 AM||||Thanks for the offer.  <P>An "extra" dew wipe, though, gives me a reason to keep it and put it on my '85GT hanger queen that is under resto.  Among many other things, dew wipes are needed badly!<P>BTW - this 1 hour job only took a couple of days!  No bad, huh?||||reg||6
Z||000004||beer_stud_21||11-11-2001||02:52 PM||||1 hour job eh?  I need $90.00 worth of parts to do mine according to <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>GM Parts Direct</A>.  Now I just need to decide when I want to do them.  Right now I am in the middle of tearing out my interior.  Is there any reason to wait to put new dew wipes on after I repaint the car?  That way I don't accidently paint the new wipes...<P>-Marlin <p>[This message has been edited by beer_stud_21 (edited 11-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnF||11-11-2001||03:06 PM||||Put on the dew wipes while you have interior apart.  No body shop worth yu time is going to paint thge exterior dew wipes.   You are a lot more liable to damage the new paint while installing the wipes than the paint shop is to paint them!<P>CAUTION:  Order Rodney Dickman's screw remover for door wipes before you start.  Saves you a LOT of time and aggrivation.<P>review the notes & procedures at:  <A HREF="http://www.cvalley.net/~tevans/fiero/SKWYRUL_L.htm" TARGET=_blank>www.cvalley.net/~tevans/fiero/SKWYRUL_L.htm</A> <P>if my typing skill are up to snuff!||||reg||1
